rossing","pick_start":"U","pick_start_origin":"source_authored","role":"notation_practice","route":"up_and_down","source_refs":["L3-TXT1-21","L3-PDF1","L3-TXT24-24","L3-TXT225-226","L3-TXT229-243"],"tail_pause":null,"unresolved":["Authored grouping count retained; explicit metrical beat-unit configuration required."]},{"accent_policy":"even","event_ids":["fg:item:000240:event:0001","fg:item:000240:event:0002","fg:item:000240:event:0003","fg:item:000240:event:0004","fg:item:000240:event:0005","fg:item:000240:event:0006","fg:item:000240:event:0007","fg:item:000240:event:0008","fg:item:000240:event:0009","fg:item:000240:event:0010","fg:item:000240:event:0011","fg:item:000240:event:0012","fg:item:000240:event:0013","fg:item:000240:event:0014","fg:item:000240:event:0015","fg:item:000240:event:0016","fg:item:000240:event:0017","fg:item:000240:event:0018","fg:item:000240:event:0019","fg:item:000240:event:0020","fg:item:000240:event:0021","fg:item:000240:event:0022","fg:item:000240:event:0023","fg:item:000240:event:0024","fg:item:000240:event:0025","fg:item:000240:event:0026","fg:item:000240:event:0027","fg:item:000240:event:0028","fg:item:000240:event:0029","fg:item:000240:event:0030","fg:item:000240:event:0031","fg:item:000240:event:0032","fg:item:000240:event:0033","fg:item:000240:event:0034","fg:item:000240:event:0035","fg:item:000240:event:0036","fg:item:000240:event:0037","fg:item:000240:event:0038","fg:item:000240:event:0039","fg:item:000240:event:0040"],"grouping":{"beat_unit_q":null,"kind":"even_subdivision","marking_factor":[1,1],"notes_per_beat":3,"source_label":"triplets per authored session grouping"},"id":"fg:variant:000833","label":"triplets-up_and_down-U-even","pick_start":"U","pick_start_origin":"source_authored","role":"notation_practice","route":"up_and_down","source_refs":["L3-TXT1-21","L3-PDF1","L3-TXT24-24","L3-TXT225-226","L3-TXT229-243"],"tail_pause":null,"unresolved":["Authored grouping count retained; explicit metrical beat-unit configuration required."]}],"workbook_id":"fg:workbook:000003"}],"schema_version":"1.0.0-curriculum-candidate","source_acceptance":"Results/primary/20260906T182131Z-2.1.1.1.1-r02-results.md","source_manifest_sha256":"e856ef05e610b9be51f33aac661a900301f747a9259bfcbd951b756a247504fe","sources":{"L3-PDF1":{"format":"pdf","page":1,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_3_Odd_Count_String_Transfer.pdf","sha256":"f04c1e49ce939ec83e5c80f9ad8cc81fd49da62e2039c25cac5367cea0fa6234","text":"108 Finger Permutations - Level 3\nOdd-Count String Transfer: 3+1 / 1+3 Split-Point Control\nLevel 2 crossed after note 2. Level 3 moves the crossing to an odd beat, changing the inside/outside geometry of alternate picking.\n1. Keep the foundation fixed\n1 = index / fret 5\n2 = middle / fret 6\n3 = ring / fret 7\n4 = pinky / fret 8\nNo position shift or string skip yet.\n2. Move the crossing point\nMode A, 3+1: cross after note 3.\nMode B, 1+3: cross after note 1.\nRun the same adjacent pairs up and down.\nThe four-digit code never changes.\n3. Separate before combining\nUse one 12-code set and one mode per session.\nRepeat with downstroke and upstroke starts.\nCombine the modes only after each is clean.\nEven tone matters more than top speed.\nMode A example - code 1234\n3+1: notes 1-2-3 on the first string; note 4 on the adjacent string.\ne|--------|--------|--------|--------|------8-|\nB|--------|--------|--------|------8-|5-6-7---|\nG|--------|--------|------8-|5-6-7---|--------|\nD|--------|------8-|5-6-7---|--------|--------|\nA|------8-|5-6-7---|--------|--------|--------|\nE|5-6-7---|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nMode B example - code 1234\n1+3: note 1 on the first string; notes 2-3-4 on the adjacent string.\ne|--------|--------|--------|--------|--6-7-8-|\nB|--------|--------|--------|--6-7-8-|5-------|\nG|--------|--------|--6-7-8-|5-------|--------|\nD|--------|--6-7-8-|5-------|--------|--------|\nA|--6-7-8-|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nE|5-------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nFIRST PASS\nLightly accent the landing note 4 after each crossing.\nSECOND PASS\nRemove the accent and make all four notes equal in volume.\nEvery exercise page includes both ascending and descending adjacent-pair routes.\nFIRST PASS\nLightly accent the landing note 2 after each crossing.\nSECOND PASS\nRemove the accent and make all four notes equal in volume.\nEvery exercise page includes both ascending and descending adjacent-pair routes.\nSession protocol\n1\nBegin 8-12 BPM below your clean Level 2 tempo.\n2\nSession A: one 12-code set in Mode A. Session B: the same set in Mode B.\n3\nPlay each exercise up and down, first with a downstroke start and then with an upstroke start.\n4\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next time. After two errors or\nrising tension, reduce 4-6 BPM.\n5\nAdvance when both mode pages are clean on two separate days; then\ntry alternating 3+1 and 1+3 between successive string pairs.\nStandard tuning. Fifth position. Preserve code order; cross after note 3 in Mode A or after note 1 in Mode B.\nPage 1 of 19\n","text_sha256":"0e2d8b020cb3e4b6ada33894f310bbc06afcb280a89f569402a8f7fc49074bc9"},"L3-TXT1-21":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":21,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_3_Odd_Count_String_Transfer.txt","sha256":"1bb8d5225f2db8df2b3ce518f10f28e11158592e0b5cbbb4c28af2742c861b4f","text":"108 FINGER PERMUTATIONS - LEVEL 3: ODD-COUNT STRING TRANSFER\n3+1 / 1+3 split-point control in standard tuning.\nFifth position: 1=index/fret 5, 2=middle/fret 6, 3=ring/fret 7, 4=pinky/fret 8.\n\nMOVEMENT RULE\nMode A - 3+1 late transfer: play digits 1-3 on the first string and digit 4 on the adjacent string.\nMode B - 1+3 early transfer: play digit 1 on the first string and digits 2-4 on the adjacent string.\nAscend through E/A, A/D, D/G, G/B, B/e. Descend through e/B, B/G, G/D, D/A, A/E.\nThe four-digit code order never changes.\n\nWHY THIS IS LEVEL 3\nLevel 2 crossed after note 2. These modes cross after note 3 or note 1, so strict alternate picking produces different\ninside- and outside-string transitions depending on whether the exercise begins with a downstroke or an upstroke.\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nBegin 8-12 BPM below your clean Level 2 tempo. Use one 12-code set and one mode per session.\nPlay each exercise ascending and descending, once beginning with a downstroke and once beginning with an upstroke.\nFirst pass: lightly accent the first note after the crossing. Second pass: make all four notes equal in volume.\nRotate the existing straight-16th, triplet, and quintuplet groupings across sessions.\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next time. After two errors or rising tension, reduce 4-6 BPM.\nAdvance when both modes for the set are clean on two separate days.","text_sha256":"d7085448b76bcb825d014215d09291a04e03445a072e60dadf5bbc53b1678cce"},"L3-TXT225-226":{"first_line":225,"format":"txt","last_line":226,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_3_Odd_Count_String_Transfer.txt","sha256":"1bb8d5225f2db8df2b3ce518f10f28e11158592e0b5cbbb4c28af2742c861b4f","text":"MODE B - 1+3 EARLY TRANSFER\nDigit 1 starts on the first string; digits 2-4 continue on the adjacent string.","text_sha256":"82697abc2662128be9864060b81b8a509210ac01594df2fda47c4a45fb7e23e9"},"L3-TXT229-243":{"first_line":229,"format":"txt","last_line":243,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_3_Odd_Count_String_Transfer.txt","sha256":"1bb8d5225f2db8df2b3ce518f10f28e11158592e0b5cbbb4c28af2742c861b4f","text":"Exercise 001: 1212\nASCEND\ne|--------|--------|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|\nB|--------|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|\nG|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|\nD|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|--------|\nA|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nE|5-------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nDESCEND\ne|5-------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nB|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|--------|--------|\nG|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|--------|\nD|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|--------|\nA|--------|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|5-------|\nE|--------|--------|--------|--------|--6-5-6-|","text_sha256":"f369d1c30368c489a8da874b52d57e52736faa2f8089f0d90a955728f0e7a875"},"L3-TXT24-24":{"first_line":24,"format":"txt","last_line":24,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_3_Odd_Count_String_Transfer.txt","sha256":"1bb8d5225f2db8df2b3ce518f10f28e11158592e0b5cbbb4c28af2742c861b4f","text":"SET 1 OF 9 - EXERCISES 001-012","text_sha256":"239b1881cfc47b7066c6e07958e765815a8d0c156dd3f618706dc2d55330e51a"}}}
